language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ A merchant's measuring weight broke into n pieces of whole-pound weights summing to m; the pieces must weigh every integer from 1 to m on a balance.
given m, n : int
find weights : matrix indexed by [int(1..n)] of int(1..m)
find c : matrix indexed by [int(1..m), int(1..n)] of int(-1..1)

branching on [weights, c]

such that
$ the pieces together make up the whole weight
(sum i : int(1..n) . weights[i]) = m,
$ the pieces have distinct weights; they are listed in increasing order to break symmetry
forAll i : int(1..n-1) . weights[i] < weights[i+1],
$ each integer weight w from 1 to m is balanced by placing pieces on the two pans (c[w,i] = 1 one pan, -1 the other, 0 unused)
forAll w : int(1..m) . ((sum i : int(1..n) . c[w,i] * weights[i]) = w)
